      "lastReply": "A tiger named Raja lived deep in the Sundarbans, where he ruled with a roar but secretly envied the village feasts he smelled from afar. One monsoon evening, a kind old cook named Amma got lost in the forest and stumbled upon his den. Instead of fear, she saw his longing eyes and offered a deal: she'd teach him to cook if he promised never to hunt near her village again.\n\nRaja's first attempts were disasters—burnt rice, raw meat, spices everywhere but the pot. But Amma was patient, showing him how to layer flavours, seal the pot with dough, and let the dum work its magic. Slowly, his claws learned gentleness, his nose learned balance, and his heart learned joy beyond the hunt.\n\nMonths later, Raja hosted the forest's first biryani feast. Deer, monkeys, even the sceptical leopard came. As they ate under the stars, Amma smiled from the edge of the clearing. The tiger who once took had learned to give, and the forest had never tasted anything so good.\n\n7:42 PM",
